  <data name="$Terms and Conditions" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>[K]Product Intended Use: Clearly define the intended use of the OCT device, including any limitations or specific conditions for use.
Product Warranty: Outline the warranty coverage provided for the OCT device, including the duration, scope, and process for claiming warranty services.
Limitations of the Device: Clearly state any limitations, risks, or potential side effects associated with the use of the OCT device.
Regulatory Compliance: Ensure that the OCT device complies with all relevant regulatory standards and requirements, and inform users about any necessary certifications.
Intellectual Property: Specify the ownership and protection of intellectual property related to the OCT device, including patents, trademarks, and copyrights.
User Responsibilities: Detail the responsibilities of users when operating or maintaining the OCT device, including proper usage, storage, and maintenance.
Data Privacy and Security: Address how user data collected by the OCT device will be handled, stored, and protected to ensure user privacy and comply with data protection laws.
Service and Support: Describe the availability of customer support and service for the OCT device, including contact information and response times.
Product Modifications: Specify whether users are allowed to modify or alter the OCT device and any consequences for doing so.
Liability and Indemnification: Clearly define the limitations of liability for the manufacturer and specify instances where users may indemnify the manufacturer.
Dispute Resolution: Outline the procedures for resolving any disputes related to the OCT device or the terms and conditions.
Governing Law: Specify the governing law that applies to the terms and conditions and the OCT device's use.
Termination: Define the circumstances under which the manufacturer may terminate or suspend access to the OCT device or its services.
Updates and Changes: Specify how updates or changes to the device's software or firmware will be communicated to users.
Acceptance of Terms: Require users to explicitly accept the terms and conditions before using the OCT device.</value>
